LAWS REQUIRED: associative
   integers under max
     associative: True
     identity:    True   it is -3
     inverses:    False   none for -2, -1, 0
     commutative: True
   positive integers 1..6 under +
     associative: True
     identity:    False   none in the sample
     inverses:    False
     commutative: True
   nonempty strings under concatenation (sample)
     associative: True
     identity:    False   none in the sample
     inverses:    False
     commutative: False   fails at 'a', 'b'
   integers under − (the non-example)
     associative: False   fails at -3, -3, -3
     identity:    False   none in the sample
     inverses:    False
     commutative: False   fails at -3, -2
   max and + on positives are semigroups without identity; strings are a semigroup
   that is not commutative; subtraction is not a semigroup at all.
